 "_doc": "Caliche (world/Town.ts, the diner's area). The deputy's car: the Fairheaven LT '80 Cop Cruiser in the sheriff's livery (Tools/freemodels/repaint.py) in place of the exported boxes, in the car's own terms so it stands where S47Town puts it (at the office while he is in, on the highway's shoulder north of town for event 12). Its driver's door opens when the story shows the exported open door; its roof lights flash while it stands out there. The gas station: Tom's own Blender model (~/Assets/signal47-free/own/gas_station) over the exported one, on its footprint (the night window's picture, the door, the pumps and the sign keep their things to use); the pumps' faces, the canopy's tubes and the sign's faces are hidden, the old canopy lamp replaced by a warm fluorescent pool matching the local concept pass, the tubes and the sign lit while the canopy's flood slot is. One payphone (Tom, 9 November): stationPayphone at the corner of the office, on the exported call anchor that its interaction, ring and calls use (S47StationPhone cuts the old exported phone out); the second blue phone on the east curb by the souvenir shop is gone. CALICHE-HOMES (9 November): Earl's pickup by his house (H06) and a junker behind the trailer (H08), as S47CalicheNewHomes has them.",
